  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>18.3 Composite Functions</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>\(f(x)={@Fn1@}\)</p>

<p>\(g(x)={@Fn2@}\)</p>
<p><br></p>
<p>Find \(f({@sub1@})\). We will call this answer \(a\). Then find \(g(a)\) by substituting your answer into \(g(x)\)</p>

<p>\(a\)=[[input:ans1]] \(g(a)\)= [[input:ans2]][[validation:ans1]]&nbsp;[[validation:ans2]]</p>

<p>[[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>[[feedback:prt2]]</p>

<p>Find \(g({@sub1@})\). We will call this answer \(b\). Then find \(f(b)\)<br></p>

<p>\(b\)=[[input:ans3]] \(f(b)\)= [[input:ans4]][[validation:ans3]]&nbsp;[[validation:ans4]]</p>

<p>[[feedback:prt3]]</p><p>[[feedback:prt4]]</p>

<p>Find algebraically \(f(g(x))\), simplifying your answer. Then find\(f(g({@sub1@}))\).</p>
<p>Bear in mind that \(f(g({@sub1@}))\) should be equal to one of your previous answers!</p>
<p>\(f(g(x))\) =[[input:ans5]]&nbsp;\(f(g({@sub1@}))\) =[[input:ans6]]</p>
<p>[[validation:ans5]][[validation:ans6]]</p>
<p>[[feedback:prt5]]</p>
<p>[[feedback:prt6]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
